{"id": "tea:pasupatabrahma-upanisad:1-ahimsa", "source": "src:pasupatabrahma-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1 (ahiṃsā)"}, "paraphrase": "Non-injury is the sacrifice of dharma; the paramahaṃsa is its priest.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:inner-sacrifice"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pasupatabrahma-upanisad:1-inner-sacrifice", "source": "src:pasupatabrahma-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1 (inner sacrifice)"}, "paraphrase": "Rudra-Paśupati is the doer of the inner sacrifice; its fire is the haṃsa 'so'ham', its thread the praṇava; attention to nāda is the rite; without meditation on haṃsa and praṇava there is no liberation.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:inner-sacrifice", "cpt:hamsa"], "practices": ["prc:nadanusandhana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pasupatabrahma-upanisad:1.1-5", "source": "src:pasupatabrahma-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.1-5"}, "paraphrase": "Vaiśravaṇa, son of Brahmā and a Vālakhilya, asks Svayambhū about the supreme; Oṃ's measures and the three deities — Rudra (tamas), Viṣṇu (sattva), Brahmā (rajas) — are explained.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "sound-language"], "teachers": ["tch:vaisravana", "tch:brahma"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pasupatabrahma-upanisad:2.18-19", "source": "src:pasupatabrahma-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.18-19"}, "paraphrase": "Māyā exists only from the standpoint of empirical usage; in truth there is none.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
